Short:        Game controllers prefs, through GFOpenInput
Uploader:     (filled in at upload time)
Author:       AmiCradle Team
Type:         util/wb
Version:      0.2
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Distribution: Aminet

GFOpenPrefs Gamepads shows every game controller GFOpenInput (gfopeninput.library)
sees: Amiga joysticks and CD32 pads, USB pads, and pads on AmiCradle.

- The list, live: name, maker, connected or not, and where each comes from.
- Test: every button lights as it is pressed, labelled with the pad's own
  names; the sticks and triggers move; Rumble for pads that have it.
- Map...: press each button as asked (Skip what the pad lacks), and the
  pad works in every GFOpenInput program and SDL game.
- Let older games see modern pads: an opt-in patch (off by default) so
  games that read the joystick port through lowlevel.library see a modern
  pad as a CD32 pad or a joystick.

GadTools. Needs gfopeninput.library 1.2.

